2. Third-party components
-------------------------

The extension package also contains software and data that is not Kitsumi's,
under open licences that grant you rights this licence cannot take away.
Section 1 does not apply to those components. Each is governed by its own
licence, and those licences prevail over anything here.

Every one of them is listed, with its licence and the path to the full licence
text inside the package, in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt. The same list is readable
inside the extension at Settings, About & legal, Third-party licences. In
summary:

  Tesseract.js; the Tesseract OCR engine compiled to
  WebAssembly, which links Leptonica, libpng and libtiff;
  and the Japanese vertical recognition data                Apache License 2.0

  fflate                                                    MIT

  Kanji usage frequency data, by Dmitry Shpika, modified    CC BY 4.0

Dictionaries downloaded through Kitsumi are not part of the package. They are
fetched from third-party hosts at the user's request, and each keeps whatever
licence its publisher gave it.

Fonts and word packs downloaded through Kitsumi are not part of the package
either. Each font keeps its own licence (SIL Open Font License 1.1, or Apache
License 2.0 for Kosugi Maru). The word packs for Advanced scanning are derived
from JMdict (Electronic Dictionary Research and Development Group) and
CC-CEDICT (MDBG) and are shared under CC BY-SA 4.0; see the README at
https://github.com/Olexify/KitsumiOPS.


