6. Use of the software
----------------------

Kitsumi is a tool. It hosts no video, no subtitles and no dictionaries, and it
supplies no copyrighted content of its own. What it shows you comes from the
page you are on, from files you provide, or from third-party services you
choose to enable.

You are responsible for having the right to access that material, and for
complying with the terms of the sites and services you use Kitsumi with.

The same applies to files you add to Kitsumi yourself - subtitle files,
dictionaries, fonts: they stay on your device, and you are responsible for
having the right to use them. The copyright holder does not check, supply or
license them.

Custom subtitle providers. Kitsumi lets you add a subtitle site of your own
choosing (Settings, Subtitle providers, Custom providers). A custom provider is
not part of Kitsumi: the copyright holder does not make, check, endorse,
supply or support it, and has no control over the site it contacts. By adding
one you accept that:
  - you alone chose it, and you alone are responsible for checking that the
    site is genuine, lawful and safe;
  - you are responsible for having the right to use that service and anything
    it provides, under its own terms and the laws that apply to you, copyright
    included;
  - everything the provider sends or receives - your searches, any key you give
    it, and every file you download through it - is between you and that site;
  - sections 4 and 5 apply to custom providers in full, and, to the maximum
    extent permitted by applicable law, the copyright holder is not liable for
    any loss or damage caused by a custom provider or by anything obtained
    through one, and any claim a third party makes because of a custom provider
    you added is your responsibility, not the copyright holder's.
Kitsumi records on your device when you accepted this for each custom
provider you add.


